course: dictionary
lesson: 341
title: Annoy, annoyed and annoying
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: To annoy someone is to make them a little angry or fed up. Annoy is a verb, so it changes its ending: annoys, annoyed, annoying. «That's what annoys me most!» Here annoys shows what makes the speaker feel fed up.
explain: Look at the ending to find out who or what is doing the feeling. Annoyed is the feeling inside a person: «Sam was annoyed with his little brother.» Annoying is the thing or person that causes the feeling: «The buzzing fly is really annoying.»
explain: Use context to check your meaning. Swap in «made me a bit fed up» and see if the sentence still makes sense. Annoy usually means a small irritation, not a huge anger.
fact: To annoy someone means to make them a little angry or fed up.
fact: Annoyed describes a person feeling a bit angry, as in «annoyed with someone» or «annoyed about something».
fact: Annoying describes the thing or person that causes the feeling, as in «really annoying».
fact: Regional words: «bruv» (London) means brother or mate; «peak» (London) means bad luck or annoying; «grand» (Ireland) means fine.
fact: A song can be beautiful to one person and annoying to another, because taste depends on age, culture and memories.
exercise: «The buzzing fly is really annoying.» What does annoying describe? | The person who feels angry | A sunny day | *The thing that causes the feeling | A kind of bee
exercise: «Sam was annoyed with his little brother.» Who feels annoyed? | Nobody at all | The family dog | *Sam | His little brother
exercise: «A song can be beautiful to one person and annoying to another.» Why can the same song be both? | Annoying means the song is loud | Songs are all the same length | Only grown-ups can hear music | *Tastes depend on age, culture and memories
test: In «Mia was annoyed when the bell rang», which form names the feeling? | annoy | annoys | *annoyed | annoying
test: «That's what annoys me most!» What does annoys mean here? | *Makes me a bit fed up | Makes me sleepy | Makes me hungry | Makes me very happy
exam: «Interrupting people is so ___ that Ellie sighed.» Choose the best word. | annoyed | *annoying | annoys | annoy
